  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\n\nModel guidance shows upper level ridging fully moving into our\nregion on Thursday and likely staying put through the upcoming\nweekend. This will lead to gradual drying and mostly clear skies\nwhile temperatures slowly rise closer to the normal range for the\nsouth-central Arizona lower deserts. The western lower deserts \nmay reach 100 degrees again starting Friday, but for the eastern \nhalf of Arizona some reinforcing cooler air from the east Friday \nthrough Saturday should keep daytime highs at or just above 90 \ndegrees through Saturday. This cooler easterly flow may even \ncontinue into early next week with temperatures in the Phoenix \narea staying right near seasonal normals for early October.",
